from pathlib import Path
import csv, json, html

p = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
e = html.escape
rows = list(csv.DictReader((p/'replacement-map.csv').open(encoding='utf-8-sig')))
inventory = json.loads((p/'reviewed-inventory.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def pair(a,b,left,right,cls=''):
    return f'<div class="pair {cls}"><figure><img src="{a}" alt="{e(left)}"><figcaption>{e(left)}</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="{b}" alt="{e(right)}"><figcaption>{e(right)}</figcaption></figure></div>'
page = '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Rowan & Mayumi — Artwork review</title>
<style>body{margin:0;background:#eee7d8;color:#293e48;font:17px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:36px}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia;color:#284d58}h1{font-size:38px}section{margin:32px 0;padding:24px;background:#fffaf0;border:1px solid #c9b99b;border-radius:12px}.tag{color:#79613d;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}figure{margin:0}img{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:7px;background:#d8dbd3}figcaption{padding:8px 0;font-size:15px}.sprites img{height:650px;object-fit:contain}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd0b8}td{overflow-wrap:anywhere}th{background:#e9dfcc}a{color:#245c73}input{padding:12px;width:90%;margin:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700}li{margin:8px 0}.note{background:#e5eadf;padding:16px;border-left:4px solid #76896c}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:14px}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style><main>
<p class="tag">APPROVAL REVIEW · NO GAME CHANGES</p><h1>Rowan & Mayumi: consistent artwork</h1>
<p>The main issue is a combination of drawing style and sprite scale. Mayumi has softer, more realistic rendering, while Rowan has stronger drawn outlines. The game also displays Rowan at roughly 1.55 times the generic sprite height used for Mayumi, making her appear farther away.</p>
<p><strong>287 files reviewed · 36 referenced files proposed for correction · 2 new artwork previews</strong><br>The inventory includes 284 raster files and three legacy SVG placeholders. Duplicate formats, reference sheets, unused drafts and unrelated assets are included in the audit, not counted as artwork needing replacement.</p>
<p class="note">These are approval previews. Original assets, story, dialogue, choices, relationship values, saves and game code remain unchanged. The staging comparison is a separate mockup, not an implemented game screenshot.</p>
<section><h2>1. Conversation scale and style</h2><p>Keep Rowan’s approved sprite. Bring Mayumi to the same apparent conversational depth while preserving a natural height difference. Normalize head scale and body anchors rather than making both characters the same height.</p>
'''
page += pair('before-scene.png','after-scene-preview.png','Before — current game screenshot','Proposed — corrected Mayumi style and conversation scale')
page += '<p>The mockup uses a neutral expression to demonstrate the design. The final expression for “Did you answer?” should be concerned. Its simplified dialogue panel is only for context; no interface redesign is proposed.</p></section><section><h2>2. Mayumi sprite standard</h2><p>Preserve her mature face, brown eyes, low bun, jewelry, embroidered cream blouse, sage skirt and sandals. Use clearer linework and restrained shading that sits naturally beside Rowan. Apply the approved result to all seven expressions and preserve their different poses.</p>'
page += pair('../../assets/portraits/mayumi-v2/neutral.png','mayumi-style-preview.png','Before — existing neutral Mayumi','Proposed neutral style preview — full body, transparent background','sprites')
page += '<p><a href="../../assets/portraits/rowan-upgraded/concerned.png">Unchanged Rowan reference</a> · <a href="STYLE-STANDARD.md">Proposed shared art standard</a></p></section><section><h2>3. Dinner CG comparison</h2><p>Match both faces and linework while retaining the interrupted dinner, bread, seating, clothing, room and warm nighttime lighting. Mayumi’s seated distance already works here.</p>'
page += pair('../../assets/cg/chapter-two/father-continuation-v1/dinner-interrupted.webp','dinner-style-preview.png','Before — dinner interrupted','Proposed — shared character rendering')
page += '''</section><section><h2>4. Project-wide findings</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Mayumi’s seven sprites:</strong> unify face, hair and fabric rendering. Keep her age and individuality; she should not become a female version of Rowan.</li>
<li><strong>Mayumi CGs:</strong> match the family dinner, birthday, father reveal and porch artwork. Correct the blue floral skirt patch in the father-reveal CG to her established sage skirt; leave Lola and Enrich untouched.</li>
<li><strong>Intentional distance:</strong> retain Mayumi’s position facing the porch door. Keep plausible seated spacing in dinner and birthday scenes.</li>
<li><strong>Rowan:</strong> retain the ten current upgraded sprites as the adult standard. Selected CGs need small face, eye or linework corrections. Preserve the age-eleven set, intentional chibi proportions and alternate gallery outfits.</li>
<li><strong>Lighting:</strong> check nighttime sprite grading against each background. Preserve warm light on hair and skin; avoid applying a second dark filter to artwork already painted for night.</li>
<li><strong>Gallery and previews:</strong> some gallery pictures use separate cropped reference sheets. Track those alongside live assets so an old crop does not remain after an approved replacement.</li>
<li><strong>Historical assets:</strong> keep old drafts, shorter-leg versions, alternate garden outfits, source sheets and placeholders intact. Do not reactivate them.</li>
</ul></section><section><h2>5. Planned replacement map</h2><p>Each entry below has a new versioned destination. Existing files stay at their current paths as preserved originals. No destination has been installed. After approval, update the relevant scene, gallery and preview references together, and verify them on desktop.</p><p><a href="replacement-map.csv">Download the 36-file replacement map</a></p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Current asset</th><th>Proposed asset</th><th>Required correction</th><th>Referenced by</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''
for r in rows:
    page += '<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(v)+'</td>' for v in r.values())+'</tr>'
page += '</tbody></table></div></section><section><h2>6. Complete audit</h2><details><summary>Show all 287 reviewed files, including retained and archived assets</summary><input id="search" placeholder="Filter by filename, status or review note" aria-label="Filter inventory"><div class="scroll"><table id="inventory"><thead><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Decision</th><th>Review</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
for r in inventory:
    page += '<tr><td><a href="../../'+e(r['path'])+'">'+e(r['path'])+'</a></td><td>'+e(r['status'])+'</td><td>'+e(r['review'])+'</td></tr>'
page += '</tbody></table></div></details><p>Inspection sheets: '+ ' · '.join(f'<a href="sheet-{i:02}.jpg">{i}</a>' for i in range(1,12))+'</p><p><a href="reviewed-inventory.json">Full inventory data</a> · <a href="preview-prompts.txt">Preview generation notes</a></p></section><p><strong>Approval needed:</strong> approve the proposed Mayumi style, conversation scale and dinner rendering before final artwork production and replacement.</p></main><script>document.querySelector("#search").addEventListener("input",e=>{const q=e.target.value.toLowerCase();document.querySelectorAll("#inventory tbody tr").forEach(r=>r.hidden=!r.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q))})</script></html>'
(p/'review.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
print(f'Created review.html: {len(rows)} replacement entries, {len(inventory)} inventory entries')
